  "date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "Random Input, whbeers' re-creation of the Dallas Arbiter Fuzz Face (whbeers/random_input at 723a89d, hardware/random_input.kicad_sch v0.27, CC0 1.0) as published: two NPN transistors direct-coupled – Q1's collector on Q2's base, Q2's emitter fed back to Q1's base through 100 kΩ –, their collector resistors as trimmers (TRIM1 100K, TRIM2 50K) for the bias, the 470 Ω output divider, the B1K fuzz pot with 22 µF, a 2u2 input with an A100K input volume, a 10n output into the A250K volume; the effect board of the Noise Floor platform, fed at its connector E1. Transcribed for edakit's tests.",
  "purpose": {
   "use": "private",
   "market": "EU",
   "notes": "The author publishes the board for builders who order and build it for themselves. The transcription is a test of edakit, not a product."
